 "review": {
  "score": 7.0,
  "round": 1,
  "problems": [
   "At hip/waist height next to the person (about 55 px vs about 105 px) it sits at the bottom of the 'waist to chest' range and looks small and sparse in the wide shot",
   "The branches are smooth tubes of even thickness with round knob tips, which looks a little like pipe-cleaners or candy rather than branching stony coral",
   "The spec's purple fan (the #9a6bd6 poly from y -30 to -148) and its vein lines can't be seen in the rendered sheet, and the sheet shows teal and pink branches the spec doesn't contain. The render and the JSON may not match, so check that the right file was previewed",
   "There are only 3 main stems, and they branch little at the top, so the cluster's silhouette is thin"
  ]
 },
 "for": "a colourful branching coral cluster about waist to chest high",
 "source": "minted",
 "created": "2026-11-02",
